# Story 28: Scrollback & Scrolling (40s)
# Hook: Long output scrolls off the top? Walk back through every line.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-028-scrollback-scrolling.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Long output scrolls off the top? Walk back through every line.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh and generate a wall of output so we have a real scrollback buffer to explore.

[00:08.0 --> 00:14.0]
Each pane keeps its own scrollback. Let's fill it up.

[00:14.0 --> 00:22.0]
PageUp scrolls the active pane up one full page, PageDown brings you back down a page at a time.

[00:22.0 --> 00:30.0]
For fine control, Shift+Up and Shift+Down move a single line per press.

[00:30.0 --> 00:37.0]
Home snaps to the very top of the buffer, and End drops you straight back to the live prompt.

[00:37.0 --> 00:40.0]
Page, line, top, bottom -- you never lose a line of history.

